lunduke-about (0.9-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * X properties are indexed only when format is 32 and the type matches.
    UTF8_STRING titles require format 8. A short buffer is not read as Atom[].
  * An AppRow stays in the list while its Force Close menu is posted.
    The supporters idle and the Force Close refresh timeout are disconnected
    on window close.
  * Force Close is pinned to the refresh-time command and start time, signals
    with pidfd_send_signal when the kernel provides it, and re-checks start
    time on every descendant. Other rows are not signalled. A skipped kill
    shows an error. The dialog shows the command, and a foreign WM_CLASS
    does not mark another process protected.
  * Dock, desktop, utility, and skip-taskbar processes that have no Normal
    window get a row so their RssAnon is subtracted from LCOS System.
  * Oversized _NET_WM_ICON frames are skipped by offset. The icon cache
    tracks pid and a property fingerprint, and a cleared icon returns to the
    generic image.
  * Each /proc sample is paired with starttime around the status read. A
    recycled pid is dropped instead of inheriting another process's RAM.
  * The 3s timer does not start another scan while one is running, and the
    next scan waits until 3s after the last snapshot. Force Close may still
    refresh once it finishes.
  * An empty or missing _NET_CLIENT_LIST tries _NET_CLIENT_LIST_STACKING and
    then a depth-capped walk to WM_STATE clients.
  * LCOS System counts each RssAnon once and shows 0 when shared pages would
    make the remainder negative. The unclamped figure stays in the tooltip.
  * /etc/os-release is shown whenever it parses. The live-image recipe path
    is not compiled in. GDK_BACKEND is left alone; a display that cannot be
    opened prints the Needs X11 explanation.
  * Logic tests cover property format, identity match, row removal, icon
    chunks, meminfo, and os-release. The Debian build runs meson test.
  * Meson project version remains 0.9.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0000

lunduke-about (0.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Refresh the application list in short idle slices so the window stays
    responsive. Force Close rechecks only that window's XID plus the
    existing /proc command and start time.
  * Cache window icons per XID, cap _NET_WM_ICON reads, and reject
    malformed frames that would loop. Read RssAnon once; do not read VmSize.
  * App rows include descendant RssAnon unless that descendant has its own
    row. Windows with no PID show an em dash. The system remainder is not
    clamped to 0.
  * App-list labels stay dark on the white list background.
  * Supporter names crawl, or the header grows to one line, when the cap
    is shorter than a line. The crawl redraws only when the text moves and
    pauses while the pointer is over the names.
  * CPU, GPU, and window titles have tooltips. Rows prefer the application
    name and put the document title in the tooltip.
  * One row per process, preferring the active window. Protected classes
    are combined across that process's windows. Splash, menu, tooltip,
    notification, and utility windows are skipped.
  * List scroll position is restored after the new height exists.
  * GPU detection reads sysfs and pci.ids, prefers a 3D controller when a
    VGA device is also present, skips glxinfo at startup, and caches the
    name.
  * The refresh timer stops while the window is unmapped or iconified.
  * RAM labels use one human formatter so the rounded used and free figures
    match Built-in Memory.
  * Protected rows show a disabled menu with the reason. Session binaries
    also match /proc comm. One Force Close menu is reused.
  * A non-X11 display shows a Needs X11 row. The client list is read to
    the end.
  * Meson project version remains 0.9.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 06:33:00 +0000

